  "script": "Why do we forget what we were about to say? You walk into a room, stop for a second, and realise you have absolutely no idea why you are there.\n\nSurprisingly, this happens because your brain treats a doorway as the start of a new event. The old room is filed away, and the thought you were holding goes with it. That is why it feels like the idea simply vanished.\n\nThere is a fix, and it is almost too simple. Say the thing out loud before you move. The words survive the doorway, and so does the thought. The experiment is over.",
